  "proof": "The consecutive turn determinants are $73t,55,95t,168t-55$, and the edge-to-origin determinants are $70t-29,29,40,98t-40$. With four vertices, positivity of the turns puts both other vertices strictly to the left of each edge, giving the strict convex counterclockwise polygon. A clockwise cyclic order is impossible because one turn is $55$. Positivity of the edge-to-origin determinants is then exactly the interior condition. These inequalities reduce to $t>29/70$. The moving vertex has first margin negative and second margin positive, and its third margin is $2t-1$. All other margins are nonzero and constant, so the sole seam is $t=1/2$.\n\nUsing the edge intersections from the level test and the cyclic shoelace formula gives $k=84t$ and\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nQ_1&=\\frac{24463t^2-16282t+2695}{2(17t-6)(17t-5)},&\n\\sigma_1&=\\frac{(17t-7)(168t-55)}{(17t-6)(17t-5)},\\\\\nQ_2&=\\frac{2520t^2-1313t+198}{2(15t-1)},&\n\\sigma_2&=\\frac{130t-33}{15t-1}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nFor $29/70<t\\le1/2$, $Q_3=584t/[5(5-2t)]$ and $\\sigma_3=292t/[5(5-2t)]$. For $t\\ge1/2$, $Q_3=(1680t^2+802t+55)/[10(2t+5)]$ and $\\sigma_3=(548t-55)/[5(2t+5)]$. The two branches agree at the seam. To obtain the chords from the intersection pairs, take the absolute second-coordinate difference for $v_1$ and first-coordinate difference for $v_2,v_3$. For $v_3$ the Euclidean length contributes the same $\\sqrt2$ factor as the normal norm.\n\nSet $E=E_1$, $R=R_1$ from the spectral level test. The lower-branch reduced denominators, up to positive constants, are $(17t-7)(130t-33)^2(168t-55)$ and $(17t-7)^4(130t-33)^6(168t-55)^4$ for $E,R$ respectively. The upper-branch denominators multiply these by $(548t-55)^2$ and $(548t-55)^6$ respectively. Every factor is positive in its branch. The lower-branch numerator degrees are $5,18$. Substitute $t=(29/70+s/2)/(1+s)$ and multiply by $(1+s)$ to the respective degree. For the upper branch, remove the positive factors $t,t^3$ from the two numerators of remaining degrees $7,23$, then substitute $t=(1+s)/2$. In each case clear rational coefficient denominators with a positive multiplier and divide by the positive integer gcd. The resulting ascending coefficient vectors are as follows.\n\n```text\nLE = [422796902567017, 3358136541863551, 10565310444580458,\n16477933266907630, 12751244687684125, 3920983436755875]\n\nLR = [5970784818454267377722209041711580777446073569,\n189204516510098650263153566970374421592496416410,\n2802584086314728716066527483421304197772379257905,\n25804020898542747399847558238391093950342877479504,\n165600597694471811576303565600104374901461993888660,\n787096523640627553007157724613343087273757268426680,\n2872844754406066507670307056163665684956309239281156,\n8236905134669610438788752000263137545285618140411760,\n18814073317509287482223067563736875890234087966083150,\n34502956461260885746542376823759498966740094508757500,\n50939201666480652829308443416392334241734704231318750,\n60417795008396169136232682591355973557429986921550000,\n57157538750150372438785333032533006983206864037062500,\n42555461490386901975043404215394684403360096466875000,\n24392240239853549525526093965956227019409312570312500,\n10388386883054263109166317939879606237330162656250000,\n3096268268729776804271727546659473776172099697265625,\n576441361793502562668278113430008636720981347656250,\n50459939131382474748818019592605726944181884765625]\n\nUE = [3678590279691, 43334364515706, 210147200836272,\n542384380155930, 801614235827313, 675616374100540,\n299033667304900, 53835897024000]\n\nUR = [10428984397449037661531494543601401671921,\n449113516943583489360034588959331385007669,\n9119982910234259280197145953426916393000090,\n116203429770272791377175575035611090287385446,\n1042878085344873848005469178553665363271076343,\n7015130534072522324587320816131891495847011211,\n36748090226654129634162098270291066254339943028,\n153761089552207489735525632386088995953514739120,\n522990620429062118914222721483597249550203823327,\n1464033799604278390852552091732446303074986477451,\n3402378327308850313250415880495468501870407466794,\n6602513886357499217214257004126949000616730716814,\n10735033018323470981677695514037204337999268696905,\n14640540723323801461649060790743084817921955305381,\n16727892700428062257221063285743378621564201437608,\n15949551177766271158543714127735423551467260459004,\n12598040446334692921237168433138707682638248152080,\n8146907980603958039755252701860257370922372318000,\n4236739662196605968188813670024538475506578592000,\n1724782906668215580528450016766846026239100840000,\n527543012057657160143599350758350932462566400000,\n113440121787597873623189294152598273249280000000,\n15190454634290761825967363017891510026240000000,\n944871609441662220571687119026021990400000000]\n```\n\nEvery listed coefficient is positive, giving $E,R>0$ on each open branch and at the seam by the upper branch. Apply the level test. Its determinant identity at $r=1$, equivalently $\\det(I-B)=(4-\\sum_i f_i^2-f_1f_2f_3)/4$, also gives the cubic inequality.\n",
