  "statement": "Let $K_t=\\operatorname{conv}\\{(7-17t,-6+15t),(1,-5),(7,-6),(2,4)\\}$. For every $t>29/70$, the listed polygon is strictly convex in the listed cyclic order with the origin in its interior. Set $v_1=(1,0),v_2=(0,1),v_3=(-1,-1)$, $k=|K_t|$, $Q_i=|K_t\\cap\\{v_i\\cdot x\\ge0\\}|$, and $\\sigma_i=\\mathcal H^1(K_t\\cap\\{v_i\\cdot x=0\\})/\\lVert v_i\\rVert$. Define $f_i=2\\sqrt{kQ_i}/(\\sigma_i\\sum_jQ_j/\\sigma_j)$ and let $J$ be the largest eigenvalue of the zero-diagonal symmetric matrix with cyclic entries $f_i/2$. Then throughout $t>29/70$,\n$$J<1,\\qquad \\sum_i f_i^2+f_1f_2f_3<4.$$\nThe stated parameter range is the whole strict convex, interior-origin domain in the listed order.",
